isky because it’s a corner and black could try to trap king with king on g4 and pawns advancing. f1 is safer and centralizes king slightly for potential endgame activity. Since my knight on f4 covers f3 and h5 squares, f1 might allow future support from the knight. So **K: g2-f1** seems safest.\n\n**Answer:** K: g2-f1'}
