roach.\n\nPromising moves:\n- K: d5-e5: Moves directly toward black king, maintaining central control.\n- K: d5-e4: Moves diagonally closer to black king, also good.\n- K: d5-d6: Moves away, less aggressive.\n- K: d5-c5: Moves laterally, not directly toward black king.\n\nReason: In king endgames, opposition is crucial. By moving to e5, White places the king directly in front of Black's king on the same file (e5 vs e1), gaining distant opposition (with 3 squares between). This makes it harder for Black to advance and allows White to possibly gain closer opposition on subsequent moves. It's the most active move toward the opponent's king, which is generally best in such simplified endgames. Other moves like e4 are also reasonable, but e5 keeps the king more centralized and on a light square (if that matters, but not really here). Since it's a draw anyway, this move is as good as any, and it applies psychological pressure by advancing.\n\nAnswer: K: d5-e5"}
